  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Exact checkpoint order",
      "items": [
        "memory-index → rotate-log → rotate-roadmap → brain-index → roadmap-overview → gate → commit → push.",
        "Steps 2–5 write project records only when their sources exist.",
        "Source: engine/memory-checkpoint.mjs. The checkpoint invokes git push; the last arrow represents its result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Demo boundary",
      "items": [
        "The example uses --dry-run to preview the checkpoint. It lists steps without executing them.",
        "SessionStart reports FAIL but does not block the agent. The normal gate and memory pre-commit enforce FAIL."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading discipline",
      "items": [
        "Recall precedes index reading. Open the activity index required by the router, then only relevant lessons.",
